# holistic — the delivery package's edge route (ships beside setup/holistic-dashboard.service).
#
# WHY this file exists: the delivery chain copies the whole setup/ directory into the artifact,
# and when a service ships its OWN systemd unit (holistic-dashboard.service), emit-setup leaves
# that unit in place and generates NOTHING over it — including no route. So the edge route must
# travel in the package too, or a host on which holistic has never stood receives the unit but
# no way to reach it.
#
# WHAT it is: a naked `handle` block (a Caddy directive with no surrounding site block). The host
# edge shell imports this directory INSIDE its one site block, and a naked directive is valid only
# there — the same contract every delivered *.caddy shares. The static SPA fallback (root/file_server)
# belongs to that edge shell, so it is deliberately NOT repeated here.
#
# holistic is the landscape's own dashboard — the root app of a holistic instance. Its backend
# answers the WHOLE /api/* prefix (not the per-service /api/services/<id>/* a uniform service takes),
# so its route is a catch-all /api/* block, on the loopback port its unit declares (8770). A more
# specific /api/services/<other>/* block from another service still wins, so this coexists with them.
handle /api/* {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8770
}
